---
import ContentPage from '../components/ContentPage.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import { siteImages } from '../data/images';
const faqItems = [
  { question: 'How long do Workers last?', answer: 'Worker contracts use durations measured in days. The current table lists three days for General Worker, one day for Epic Worker, and two days for YouTube Creator Worker.' },
  { question: 'Are Worker prices permanent?', answer: 'Worker offers can change between updates, so check the hiring panel before spending Cash.' },
  { question: 'What should I know about Manual Assign?', answer: 'The hiring panel includes a Manual Assign warning. Read it before confirming a Worker contract if you prefer to assign customers yourself.' },
];
---
<ContentPage title="Karinderya Workers & Contracts" seoTitle="Karinderya Workers Guide & Contracts | Karinderya Wiki" description="Compare Karinderya worker contracts, durations, and restaurant staffing tips." kicker="Staff guide" intro="Compare temporary Worker offers and learn how contracts fit into restaurant service." relatedLinks={[{ label: 'Beginner guide', href: '/guides/beginner-guide/' }, { label: 'Equipment', href: '/equipment/' }, { label: 'Chiller', href: '/equipment/chiller/' }]} sourceIds={['worker-guide', 'worker-chiller', 'beginner-guide']} tableOfContents heroImage={siteImages.workersHero}>
  <h2 id="worker-overview">Worker Overview</h2>
  <p>Workers are temporary hires that can help operate a Karinderya. Their offers use timed contracts measured in days, so a Worker should be treated as short-term restaurant help rather than a permanent unlock.</p>

  <h2 id="worker-types">Worker Types</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Worker</th><th scope="col">Cost</th><th scope="col">Duration</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row">General Worker</th><td>&#8369;300</td><td>3 days</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Epic Worker</th><td>&#8369;1,000</td><td>1 day</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">YouTube Creator Worker</th><td>&#8369;5,000</td><td>2 days</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>

  <h2 id="hiring-workers">Hiring Workers</h2>
  <p>Worker offers show both a Cash cost and a contract duration. Check the current hiring panel before spending Cash because offers can change between game versions. When the contract ends, the Worker should no longer be treated as active restaurant staff.</p>

  <h2 id="manual-assign">Manual Assign</h2>
  <p>The hiring interface includes a warning related to Manual Assign. Read that warning before confirming a hire, especially if you prefer to assign customers yourself.</p>

  <h2 id="using-workers">Using Workers</h2>
  <p>Workers are most relevant when the restaurant has enough activity for additional help. Compare the displayed contract length and cost with the tasks you want assistance with before accepting an offer.</p>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />
</ContentPage>
